\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The opposite point}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Take the points #{0} and #{1/2} on the circle of length #{1}.
\ref{fdip-00BF} gives
#{\mathbb E\lvert f_0-f_{1/2}\rvert^2=\tanh(m/4)/m}. The
[increment metric](fdip-00CY) of the field in \ref{fdip-00BG}
therefore satisfies
##{d(0,1/2)=\sqrt{\frac{\tanh(m/4)}{m}}.}}
